@src 0:6
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Spl.) (Mains) 2004
Which of the following is not a characteristic of Indian Economy ?
(a) Low productivity of labour
(b) Lower per capita income
(c) Low rate of capital formation
(d) Lack of Natural Resources
@ans (d)
@end

Signs of underdevelopment: **low per capita income**, **low capital formation**, dependence on **agriculture**, **disguised unemployment**, high population growth and a **high dependency ratio**, and poor human capital. India is rich in natural resources, so their "lack" is not a feature.

