@q 0:8-9

**Voluntary social service** creates no income, so it is a non-economic activity. The **first generation** of reforms (1991) was **LPG**: liberalisation, privatisation, globalisation; the **second generation** (from about 2000) covered public sector, oil, power, labour and governance reforms.

@section 1.2 | Development, Growth and Measurement

@q 1:1-4

**Real income** = money income adjusted for prices, so if both double it is unchanged. **Amartya Sen** (Nobel 1998) argued that development should be **people-centred** (capabilities, health, education), not commodity-centred. The **"Hindu rate of growth"** (coined by **Raj Krishna**) was the slow **3.5%** annual growth of national income from the 1950s to the 1970s.

